	(paper "A1")
	(title_block
		(title "HIGH VOLTAGE: LT3751 flyback charger, TPS25982 eFuse, 1:50 transformer, two series rectifiers + fusible resistor, child FB ceiling")
		(date "2026-11-27")
		(rev "A-draft")
		(company "Open AED project — CERN-OHL-S-2.0 — NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION")
		(comment 1 "NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design")
		(comment 2 "Source: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md §B4; contract.md §5.5; capture notes WP-E.md")
		(comment 3 "HIGH VOLTAGE: HV_* nets reach about 2,000 V in normal use (top of the at-plan window 2,008.6 V) and up to 2,409 V if the last-resort primary-side trip is the only limit left (capacitor surge rating >= 2,420 V, D-65). Classes HV / HV_PULSE (hierarchy.toml). No test point on any HV_* net (contract R9).")
		(comment 4 "Charger runs only when VTRANS_EN (eFuse) and CHARGE_EN AND local VTRANS-good (CHARGE pin) are high; both come from sheet 09 = request AND both discharge paths proven held AND not test mode (D-25).")
		(comment 5 "Child ceiling: FB divider active only while MODE_CHILD_HW is high; open/absent contact = FB grounded = adult (D-60). MODE_HW_RB_N reads back the FB-switch gate drive.")
		(comment 6 "Generated by tools/schgen from the sheet spec — edit the spec, not this file (until schematic freeze)")
	)
