		(uuid "7a5b565a-7d7a-56ba-891a-163441094e0c")
	)
	(text_box "Each UX-F5B is rated 8 kV repetitive (Sanken rev 1.6); worst reverse voltage = capacitor 2,420 V (surge/test; the v0.3 trip top is 2,409 V) + 50 x 9.2 V = 2,880 V -> 2.8 x margin per diode; no voltage sharing is relied on\n(no grading resistors). Average current <= IPK/2N = 0.23 A vs 0.35 A rating; trr 0.15 us max is ABOVE the LT3751's < 100 ns recommendation (capture notes).\nR1004 (about 10 Ohm, high-voltage fusible) limits and then breaks a capacitor discharge into the secondary if both diodes short (R-15). No catalogue part found that states >= 3 kV across the open element: qualification\npart (footprint and MPN to be decided).\nHV_SEC, HV_D_MID, HV_RECT: class HV (12.5 mm placeholder). HV_CAP_P: class HV_PULSE. HV_RTN: class RTN_PULSE. No test points (R9)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.995 296.989 0)
		(size 250.28 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
